<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  ShokkweaveTraderStrip.xml       ShokkweaveEconomy - new file, SHOKKWEAVE_SOLE_SOURCE_1
  ============================================================================

  The sole-source strip (spec section 2). One structural kill, plus two
  non-trader leaks the ban also covers (section 6 ban 4: "from any source but
  the Webwork" - a trader is only the named example).

  1) tradeability All -> Sellable. ❓verify-at-build RESOLVED: Hyperweave (and
     its ParentName="ResourceBase") declares NO <tradeability> element at all
     (checked against the live Core install's raw XML,
     Data/Core/Defs/ThingDefs_Items/Items_Resource_Stuff.xml and
     Data/Core/Defs/ThingDefs_Items/Items_Resource_Base.xml) - the field is
     sitting on the C# default (ThingDef.cs: `Tradeability.All`), so this is a
     PatchOperationAdd, not a Replace; a Replace here would silently match
     nothing.

     MEASURED against Source/RimWorld/
     TradeabilityUtility.cs and StockGeneratorUtility.cs (RimSage, this build):
     TryMakeForStockSingle refuses (Log.Error, no Thing) any def whose
     tradeability.TraderCanSell() is false, and TraderCanSell() is true only
     for Buyable/All - never Sellable. That check runs INSIDE TryMakeForStockSingle
     itself, so it closes every route without touching a single TraderKindDef or
     StockGenerator: StockGenerator_Tag/_Category additionally pre-filter
     candidates on TraderCanSell() before they're ever chosen, and
     StockGenerator_SingleDef (the guy762 Czerka/HuttGalleon KotOR traders) has
     no such pre-filter and will still LOG AN ERROR ("Tried to make
     non-trader-sellable thing for trader stock") the first time it tries -
     harmless, but expected in the log; not a defect in this patch.
     Sellable still allows the colonist to SELL it (PlayerCanSell is true for
     Sellable) - the smuggler's-jackpot economy the sheet describes.

  2) Quest-reward strip: RewardStandardCore removed from thingSetMakerTags.
     MEASURED present on the def this build (RimSage get_def_details) - the
     ThingSetMaker pool that draws this tag is dynamic (no XML ThingSetMakerDef
     names Hyperweave directly), which is exactly why the tag is the only lever.

  3) Belt-and-braces: the ExoticMisc trade tag is also removed directly. Every
     currently-measured StockGenerator_Tag route to this def (Base_Empire_Standard,
     Base_Outlander_Standard, Caravan_Outlander_Exotic, Orbital_Exotic,
     DV_Base_Keshig_Standard, DV_Caravan_Keshig_Exotic) is reached ONLY through
     this tag, never by SingleDef name - tradeability alone already closes the
     route (StockGenerator_Tag.GenerateThings filters on TraderCanSell()), but
     the tag strip is a second independent lock: it also keeps the def off any
     future/unlisted trader that adds ExoticMisc stock by tag, and off anything
     else in the game that keys off trade tags rather than tradeability
     (colonist "sell to" UI groupings, some quest/reward pickers). Judgment
     call per the spec's own "belt-and-braces" framing - decided YES.

  4) Stuff-commonality: 0.1 -> 0.05 (owner-ruled number, 2026-09-11). Halves
     the odds shokkweave is picked as the stuff for pawn-generated or
     ThingSetMaker-rolled apparel; the raw resource sole-source holds
     regardless because tailored gear never yields the resource back out.

  Hyperweave is Core, always present, so no PatchOperationFindMod guard is
  needed on this file.

  NOT covered here (deferred, per the spec and the item's own scope):
  - Cargo/resource pod contents - ❓ rides the live-proof pass (build-order
    step 2), not this step.
  - Live trader-generation proof itself - build-order step 2, needs a
    quicktest map. Not attempted in this build.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
    <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="Hyperweave"]</xpath>
    <value>
      <tradeability>Sellable</tradeability>
    </value>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationRemove">
    <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="Hyperweave"]/thingSetMakerTags/li[text()="RewardStandardCore"]</xpath>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationRemove">
    <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="Hyperweave"]/tradeTags/li[text()="ExoticMisc"]</xpath>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
    <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="Hyperweave"]/stuffProps/commonality</xpath>
    <value>
      <commonality>0.05</commonality>
    </value>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
